<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lachlan Macquarie</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1762–1824</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lachlan Macquarie was a Scottish army officer who served as Governor of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-wales">South Wales</a> from 1810 to 1821, after the deposition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-bligh">William Bligh</a>. He restored order, built roads, churches and public buildings and sponsored the first crossing of the Blue Mountains. He favoured the readmission of freed convicts to society, which brought him into conflict with free settlers and the British government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lachlan-macquarie.jpg" alt="Lachlan Macquarie" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Opie? · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ln-Governor-Lachlan_macquarie.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
